{"slug": "types-of-thermowells", "targets": ["thermowell types"], "html": "<h2 style=\"font-size:24px;font-weight:700;color:#0186e0;margin:34px 0 16px;\">Thermowell Types by Stem Profile and Process Connection</h2><p><strong>Thermowell types</strong> are grouped in two ways besides bar stock or fabricated construction: by the shape of the stem and by how the well is fixed to the process. Choosing both correctly decides strength, response time and ease of maintenance.</p><h3 style=\"font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:#1a2b4a;margin:20px 0 10px;\">Stem Profile Types</h3><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:16px;\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Profile</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Shape</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Main feature</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Typical use</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Straight</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Same diameter along full length</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Simple and low cost</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Low velocity lines and tanks</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Tapered</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Diameter reduces gradually toward tip</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Highest stiffness and natural frequency</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">High velocity steam, gas and liquid lines</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Stepped</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Larger root, sudden step to smaller tip</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Faster response from thin tip</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Moderate velocity services needing quick response</td></tr></table></div><h3 style=\"font-size:19px;font-weight:700;color:#1a2b4a;margin:20px 0 10px;\">Process Connection Types</h3><div style=\"overflow-x:auto;\"><table style=\"width:100%;border-collapse:collapse;margin:14px 0;font-size:16px;\"><tr><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Connection</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">How it is fixed</th><th style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;background:#0186e0;color:#fff;\">Typical use</th></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Threaded</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Screwed into a threaded coupling, usually NPT</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Low to medium pressure, small lines</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Flanged</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Welded or forged flange bolted to a nozzle</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Refinery and chemical plants, easy removal</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Socket weld or butt weld</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Welded directly into the pipe</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">High pressure and high temperature service</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Van Stone</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Loose lap joint flange clamped between flanges</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Corrosive service with exotic materials</td></tr><tr><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Sanitary</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Hygienic clamp fitting with smooth surface</td><td style=\"border:1px solid #cfe3f5;padding:8px 10px;text-align:left;\">Food, dairy and pharma</td></tr></table></div><p>Whatever the type, check the well for wake frequency and stress with the ASME PTC 19.3 TW method, especially in high velocity lines.</p>"}